// Editor / language-server config ONLY — nothing in the build reads this file.
//
// Why it exists: the root tsconfig.json is the BUILD config (`npm run build` runs
// bare `tsc`, and its "rootDir": "src" / "include": ["src/**/*"] must stay that way
// or tests would be type-checked and emitted into dist/). That left tests/ outside
// the build's TypeScript program. This separate editor project keeps test call sites
// visible to language-server reference searches without changing build output.
//
// A "no references" answer that omits tests is exactly the false negative the
// "never assert a negative from a single search" rule in CLAUDE.md exists to prevent,
// so this file closes that hole rather than leaving it as a documented trap.
//
// "include" deliberately pulls in ../src as well: tsserver searches for references
// across every loaded project that CONTAINS the file being queried, so the tests
// project must contain src/ too, not just import from it.
//
// "module": "esnext" overrides the build's commonjs — tests legitimately use
// top-level await and import.meta, which commonjs rejects (TS1378 / TS1343).
// esbuild/vitest ignore "module" entirely, so this cannot change test runtime behavior.
//
// Pre-existing type errors in tests (partial mock objects) are NOT fixed here and are
// NOT gated by CI; this config exists to make tests visible to the indexer, not to
// typecheck them. Do not wire it into a CI gate without fixing those first.
{
  "extends": "../tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": "..",
    "module": "esnext"
  },
  "include": ["**/*", "../src/**/*"]
}
